 the prime  minister's numbers and the provincial  government's numbers in alberta they're  identical so it's not like the federal  government is perceived to be doing that  much better a job in fact it's doing an  equivalent job to the provincial  government and both are seen as doing an  inadequate job by that by people in the  in the province of alberta yeah what  we're seeing on the more punitive forms  of uh preventing people from from  spreading the virus and by that i mean  lockdowns  people are completely divided on that  question now it varies by region younger  people are especially not happy with  with lockdowns and when you go back to  the start of this crisis we were getting  very very high numbers of canadians who  were saying say for example not this  christmas but the previous christmas  yeah we've got to shut things down and  those numbers were in the 70s and 80s  now it's completely divided it's 50 50.  so again this is the controversy coming  back into things and things are not as  certain as they once were around this  pandemic and the management of it where  you do see really high numbers of  canadians rallying behind a particular  position it's about providing more  funding maybe even emergency funding to  our health care system to be able to  provide access to emergency services and  other types of services to be able to uh  you know get us back on track with  everything from elective surgery through  to dealing with uh dealing with with the  cova crisis so that is the one thing  people in this survey seem to be  rallying behind but everything else is  much more controversial than it was  previously
 

